Warehouse & Distribution Science — Bartholdi and Hackman (@cs-warehouse: 0, is #reference, #part-of @cs-sources) { r_1QVYHWFDZJB0PMG6V9CB2M4H10
John J. Bartholdi III and Steven T. Hackman, Georgia Institute of Technology. Warehouse & Distribution Science, release 0.98.1. [Author site](https://www2.isye.gatech.edu/~jjb/wh/book/) · [Complete 337-file-page book](https://www.warehouse-science.com/book/editions/wh-sci-0.98.1.pdf).

Read the whole published book, its questions and applicable projects. Use the analytical account of flow, handling, storage, order work, layout and capacity, then introduce the actual incompatibility and quality constraints of a chemical store. The author calls this a work in progress; an absent topic is not an implied complete chemical-handling method.

The PDF states revised 16 August 2019; the landing page lists release 17 August. Its notice permits attributed educational copying without resale and otherwise reserves rights; this is not a blanket CC licence. Identity, contents and notice were inspected on 29 October 2026. Teacher-only solutions and separately licensed software are distinct; nothing is bundled.

